const stages=[
['Newborn · 0–3 months','A gentle, responsive rhythm',['Sing a familiar song|Sit comfortably and softly sing while your baby is awake and with you.|5 min','Face-to-face hello|Hold your baby securely and talk about what you see. Pause for their responses.|5 min','Quiet story|Read a short board book aloud; the sound of your voice is the activity.|5 min'],['Caregiver: restock diaper supplies','Caregiver: ask someone for one practical favor'],[['Diaper check','Feed in response to your baby’s cues','A quiet cuddle'],['A short song together','Caregiver: water and a meal','Follow baby’s rest cues'],['Dim the room for a calm wind-down','Prepare feeding and diaper supplies','For sleep: baby on their back in a clear, firm, flat crib or bassinet']]],
['Baby · 4–11 months','Connection through everyday play',['Peekaboo time|Play gentle peekaboo with your hands. Keep fabric away from your baby’s face.|5 min','Name the world|Point out everyday objects and name them during a walk together.|10 min','Sound explorers|Make different sounds with your voice and pause to see how your baby responds.|5 min'],['Caregiver: tidy the play space','Caregiver: wash and inspect toys'],[['Diaper and feeding check','Get dressed together','A familiar song'],['Read a board book','Supervised floor play in a clear space','Follow rest and feeding cues'],['Gentle wind-down','Prepare tomorrow’s supplies','For sleep: back in a clear, firm, flat crib or bassinet']]],
['Toddler · 1–2 years','Little choices, lots of support',['Color hunt|Look together for red, blue and yellow objects. Point and name them; no small loose items needed.|10 min','Animal moves|Waddle like a duck and stretch like a cat in a clear space. Join in at your child’s pace.|10 min','Big-block building|Build together with large age-rated blocks, then count as you tidy them away.|15 min'],['Put a toy in its basket with help','Carry a soft washcloth to the laundry','Choose between two outfits'],[['Diaper or potty support','Help brush teeth','Choose clothes'],['Active play together','Put toys away with help','Share a book'],['Help tidy one toy','Wash and brush teeth with help','Story and a calm goodbye']]],
['Preschool · 3–5 years','Play, practice, repeat',['Make a story|Take turns inventing a story about a silly animal. Draw the ending with washable crayons.|15 min','Shape detectives|Find circles, squares and rectangles around home. Draw your favorite discoveries.|15 min','Indoor picnic|Let your child pick a blanket and a book. Enjoy a familiar snack together while seated.|20 min'],['Put toys in their places','Place napkins on the table','Put dirty clothes in the hamper'],[['Get dressed with support','Brush teeth with adult help','Put pajamas away'],['Snack and connection time','Choose an activity','Tidy toys together'],['Put clothes in the hamper','Wash and brush teeth with help','Read and wind down']]],
['Early school · 6–8 years','Build confidence one small job at a time',['Family comic|Draw three panels about a funny moment in your day. Read the comic together.|20 min','Nature notebook|On a supervised walk, sketch three things you notice. Leave plants and wildlife where they are.|20 min','Paper tower|Use folded paper to build the tallest freestanding tower you can. Try a new shape and compare.|20 min'],['Make the bed','Pack the school bag with a check-in','Clear their own place after meals'],[['Get dressed and brush teeth','Make the bed','Check bag and today’s plan'],['Snack and a break','Schoolwork or reading time','A small household job'],['Pack tomorrow’s bag','Brush teeth and wash','Read and wind down']]],
['Tween · 9–12 years','Growing independence, steady connection',['Design a family game|Invent a simple game with paper, rules and a score sheet. Play a round and improve one rule.|30 min','Snack co-chef|Choose a familiar no-cook snack and prepare it together. Check allergies and handle tools with adult support.|20 min','Photo scavenger hunt|Capture five textures around home. Keep people and identifying details out of photos.|20 min'],['Fold and put away their clothes','Help clear the table','Organize school materials'],[['Personal care and breakfast','Check the day’s schedule','Pack supplies'],['Take a decompression break','Plan schoolwork','Complete an agreed household job'],['Prep clothes and supplies','Agree on device wind-down','Personal care and quiet time']]],
['Teen · 13–15 years','Collaborate, listen, make room',['Playlist connection|Each choose three songs and explain what you like about them. Listen with curiosity.|20 min','Plan a budget outing|Set a pretend budget and plan an afternoon together. Compare transport, food and activity costs.|30 min','Create something together|Let your teen choose: sketch, code a small idea, write a scene or make a collage.|30 min'],['Manage an agreed laundry task','Help prepare a meal with safe tool use','Track assignments and ask for support'],[['Personal care and breakfast','Check plans and supplies','Choose one priority'],['Unwind before schoolwork','Check commitments','An agreed household contribution'],['Prepare for tomorrow','Agree on a device stopping point','Quiet time and personal care']]],
['Older teen · 16–18 years','Practice life skills with a safety net',['Life-skills dinner|Plan a simple meal, make a shopping list and prepare it together with appropriate supervision.|45 min','Future without pressure|Each name a skill you want to learn. Find one small next step your teen chooses.|20 min','Walk and talk|Take a walk together and let your teen pick the topic. Listening counts as the activity.|20 min'],['Take ownership of an agreed chore','Practice planning a weekly budget','Communicate plans and household commitments'],[['Review commitments','Personal care and breakfast','Check transport and supplies'],['Balance work, study and downtime','Complete a household contribution','Ask for help where needed'],['Plan tomorrow’s priorities','Prepare essentials','Protect time to unwind']]],
['Young adult · 19+ years','Respect, connection and shared agreements',['Shared meal check-in|Cook or share a meal. Ask what kind of support would feel helpful this week.|30 min','Learn from each other|Take turns teaching a small skill: a recipe, app feature, hobby or practical tip.|25 min','Plan a connection ritual|Choose a realistic way to stay connected: a weekly call, walk or meal. Agree on it together.|15 min'],['Agree on household contributions if living together','Manage personal appointments and commitments','Discuss shared expenses where relevant'],[['Review personal priorities','Personal care and breakfast','Check commitments'],['Balance work, study and rest','Follow through on shared agreements','Make space for connection'],['Prepare for the next day','Personal wind-down','Respect each other’s boundaries']]]
];
const additionalActivities=[["Window light chat|Hold your awake baby securely and describe light and shadows from a comfortable spot. Avoid direct sun in their eyes.|5 min", "Name a cuddle moment|With your baby awake and securely held, describe hands and feet without asking for a response. Pause at tired cues.|5 min", "Caregiver voice duet|Two caregivers can take turns saying a familiar phrase softly while baby is awake and supported. Keep it gentle.|5 min"], ["Picture-book pointing|Point at a large picture in an age-suitable board book and name it. Let your baby turn away or pause.|5 min", "Mirror hello|Use an unbroken age-rated baby mirror during supervised awake play. Talk about the reflection and follow interest.|5 min", "Toy discovery|Offer one clean large age-rated toy in a clear play space. Stay close and remove anything damaged or too small.|10 min"], ["Scribble together|Use large age-rated washable crayons with close adult supervision. Draw together without asking for a finished picture.|10 min", "Laundry helper|Invite your toddler to place soft washcloths in a basket with you. Keep detergents and cords away.|5 min", "Clap a pattern|Clap slowly, tap your knees, or wave together. Watching or making a different movement counts.|5 min"], ["Silly puppet chat|Use your hands as talking characters and invent a short conversation. Let your child direct the story.|10 min", "Picture treasure hunt|Draw three familiar objects and look for them at home together. Leave unsafe objects in place.|15 min", "Build a pretend shop|Arrange large safe toys as a pretend shop. Take turns choosing and describing items without small coins.|15 min"], ["Invent a creature|Draw an imaginary animal and decide how it moves, eats, and lives. Take turns adding a funny detail.|20 min", "Kindness postcard|Write or draw a kind message to someone you know. An adult handles addresses or sharing.|15 min", "Rhythm makers|Tap a pattern on your knees or a table and trade turns. Keep volume comfortable and passing allowed.|10 min"], ["Paper map adventure|Draw a map of a made-up island with places to visit. Explain a route and add one surprising landmark.|25 min", "Mini interview|Choose three curious questions and interview a willing family member. No recording or sharing is needed.|20 min", "Design a reading nook|Rearrange cushions in a safe spot and choose a book. Keep exits clear and avoid climbing or heavy furniture.|20 min"], ["One-page zine|Fold paper into a small booklet and fill it with a chosen interest. Keep personal details private if sharing.|30 min", "Teach me your hobby|Invite your teen to teach you one part of a hobby. Let them choose how much to explain.|20 min", "Design a quiet reset|Together choose a short playlist, sketch, walk, or other accessible break. No need to talk the whole time.|15 min"], ["Compare everyday costs|Choose a pretend weekly budget and compare two grocery or transport plans without entering financial details online.|25 min", "Try a small project|Choose a short coding, art, writing, or repair project that fits skills and safe tools. Decide one useful next step.|30 min", "Make a family recipe card|Write down a familiar recipe with a willing relative and ask about its story. Adapt dietary needs together.|25 min"], ["Shared curiosity hour|Choose a topic both of you want to understand and explore a trustworthy source together. Stop when it feels enough.|30 min", "Plan an accessible meetup|Choose a realistic time and comfortable place for a meal or walk, respecting budgets and access needs.|20 min", "Exchange one recommendation|Trade a book, film, hobby, or music suggestion and say why it matters to you. Trying it is optional.|15 min"]];
stages.forEach((stage,i)=>stage[2].push(...additionalActivities[i]));
const parentCare={
'parent-morning':['Drink some water and have an easy breakfast when you can','Wash your face, brush your teeth, and put on comfortable clothes','Take one quiet minute to breathe or notice how you feel','Choose one realistic priority; let something less urgent wait','Ask for one specific bit of help or plan a small break'],
'parent-night':['Wash up, brush your teeth, and do your usual simple skincare','Prepare one thing for tomorrow, then stop the chores','Write down one little win and anything you can leave until tomorrow','Put your phone aside for a short wind-down when possible','Choose a quiet comfort: a book, gentle stretch, music, or rest']};
const encouragement=['You can have a hard day and still be a loving parent. Both can be true.','Your child doesn’t need a flawless day. A moment of connection matters.','Small acts of care count, even when nobody claps for them.','You’re allowed to start again after a difficult moment. Repair is a little win.','A slower day is still a day full of love.','You can ask for help and still be the strong one.','Today, notice one thing you did with care. Let that count.','You don’t have to earn rest by finishing everything.','Love also looks like listening, pausing, and trying again.','Some days the win is simply showing up.','A messy house can hold a lot of beautiful memories.','You’re raising a person, not racing a deadline.','One calm breath can be the beginning of a new moment.','Progress can be quiet: one kind word, one shared laugh.'];
const funny=['Parenting: where “a quick trip” needs a packing list.','My house has two settings: suspiciously quiet and full volume.','I used to finish a thought. Now I finish someone else’s snack.','The laundry has started a family of its own.','Bedtime: the moment every child becomes a philosopher.','My coffee and I are in a long-distance relationship.','Nothing brings a family together like a missing remote.','I clean the floor so the crumbs have a fresh start.','Parenting is saying “put your shoes on” in twelve different emotions.','I live with tiny critics who rate every dinner.','The fastest way to find a lost toy is to sit down.','Today’s workout: negotiating with someone in dinosaur pajamas.','A parent’s luxury item: eating a snack without explaining it.','Silence is golden. Unless you have children. Then investigate.'];
